// expect: 5
// An unannotated record parameter read for a field through a list pattern —
// the shape tests/floors/mn-unprovable-offset carried while it floored.
//
// The row DOES close: the call passes a literal, so the element's field set
// is proven at the site. What could not see it was the specialization walk,
// which dropped the row var and compiled one body against the decl's own
// unlearned row. Keyed on the proven set, this twins and reads `slot` — 5.
// The neighbouring wrong answer is 1, `other`'s value at slot 0, which is
// what a guessed offset returns and what the floor existed to prevent.
fn peek(frames) = match frames {
  [f, ..._] => f.slot,
  [] => 0,
}

fn main(q) = peek([{other: 1, slot: 5}])
